---
code: durable-receipt-ambiguous
run: round-trip
fixpoint: executed
when-fires: a `dorc why` answering from the local receipt store found more than one document sharing the store's greatest order, so "the last one" names a cohort rather than a document. cli/engine.rs report_recorded_store, over the reading cli/main.rs acquires from the production composition root in cli/durable.rs. {count} is how many documents share that order.
why: The store's order is when the run was recorded and its ONE selection is by order, so runs recorded at one moment leave a last it cannot name. Reported rather than resolved: a tie-break on receipt identity would choose a document by the value least related to when it was written, and choosing quietly would be worse. Every member is still listed, so the reader gets the cohort rather than a pick. Remediation register (help) wanted: say that all members are listed below, that `--receipt <id>` retrieves one exactly, and that nothing was chosen on the reader's behalf.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# One MEASURED site, which is the whole fixture requirement: a run publishes a receipt only when
# its intake ADMITTED records, and a framed stream with none is NoObservation. This case is about
# the store, not this book.
foobar sync-certs /etc/nginx/certs

-- foobar.oracle.sh --
foobar__is_converged() {
   verb="$1"; shift
   case "$verb" in
   sync-certs) foobar status --certs-current -- "$1" ;;
   *) return 2 ;;
   esac
}

-- probe-results.txt --
site 0 effect=holds rc=0

-- replay --
$ dorc --book=book.sh --pre-source foobar.oracle.sh --results - < probe-results.txt
#!/bin/sh
# dorc probe (read-only): checks per-SITE convergence, mutates nothing.
# When run, emits one results-record per site on stdout (the return channel):
#   site <leafid> effect=<holds|absent|cant-tell> rc=<n>
# effect is derived from the probe command's rc (0=holds, 1=absent, else cant-tell);
# rc is the raw PROBE-command status (opaque to Dorc -- the record is the out-of-band lane).

printf 'dorc-records/1 nonce=dorc attempt=1 host=localhost book=8b1e04045b8e3486b38780d87b77c6d36b796a35e2ba5a8c656aee2d829a448f sites=1 @@dorc@@\n'
# site 0: dorc-auto:foobar@converged
foobar__is_converged() {
   verb="$1"; shift
   case "$verb" in
   sync-certs) foobar status --certs-current -- "$1" ;;
   *) return 2 ;;
   esac
}
foobar__is_converged 'sync-certs' '/etc/nginx/certs'; _rc=$?; if [ "$_rc" -eq 0 ]; then _e=holds; elif [ "$_rc" -eq 1 ]; then _e=absent; else _e=cant-tell; fi; printf 'dorc site 0 effect=%s rc=%s @@dorc@@\n' "$_e" "$_rc"
printf 'dorc-records-end/1 nonce=dorc @@dorc@@\n'
#!/bin/sh
# dorc apply: the book, with already-converged/dead lines elided (value-preserving stand-in).

#!/bin/sh
# One MEASURED site, which is the whole fixture requirement: a run publishes a receipt only when
# its intake ADMITTED records, and a framed stream with none is NoObservation. This case is about
# the store, not this book.
# foobar sync-certs /etc/nginx/certs   # dorc: elided (already converged / dead branch)

$ dorc --book=book.sh --pre-source foobar.oracle.sh --results - < probe-results.txt > /dev/null

$ dorc why --receipt-last > /dev/null
